  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement functionality. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**New module `src/statements.js` with:**\n\n**`statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)`** function that:\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` with:\n  - **invoices array** listing customer's invoices that are:\n    - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n    - issueDate on or before asOf date\n    - Each with: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n    - **due** calculated from `balanceDue()`\n    - Sorted by issueDate ascending\n  - **totalDue** as sum of all individual due amounts\n- Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` for unknown customers\n\n**Updated `issueInvoice()` and `recordPayment()`** to:\n- Preserve optional invoice metadata (terms, dueDate, voucher)\n- Keep all fields through the workflow\n\n**Key features:**\n- Filters out draft and paid invoices (only shows outstanding)\n- Includes partially paid invoices with remaining balance\n- Respects date range (asOf cutoff)\n- Accounts for vouchers in total calculation\n- Sorts for easy review\n\n**Tests:** 14 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Empty statements\n- Customer filtering\n- Status filtering (draft/paid/partial)\n- Date range filtering\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Invoice details preservation\n- Voucher calculation\n- Balance calculations\n\nAll 176 tests pass.",
